{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790724082,"nonce":"60jCluPLaNOCNOeklelfuDz+jpo=","title":"Unresolved generic stringification prints Dynamic string addresses","message":"A generic Std.string path emits haxe_value_to_string_by_tag with tag 0 when its type parameter remains unresolved. The runtime treats tag 0 as an integer, so StringBuf.add on a Dynamic string prints the pointer address. Issue9771 fails because the buffer contains two addresses rather than \"foobar\".\n\nThe unresolved slot can hold either a tagged Dynamic box, a raw scalar, or a raw static HaxeString. Dispatch boxes and scalars through haxe_std_string_ptr, and identify raw static strings before that dispatch. The focused regression covers Dynamic strings and integers through generic Std.string and StringBuf.add.\n\nReproducer: haxe-conformance/corpus/tests/unit/src/unit/issues/Issue9771.hx. Regression: haxe-conformance/regressions/GenericDynamicStringification.hx.","files":null}]}